      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $X,$ given by\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}$ on $X?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the third row to the first row.\n\nApplying this row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-3{R}_{3} \\\\  & \\sim{\\small \\begin{bmatrix}-7+(-3)(7) & 4+(-3)(7) & 3+(-3)(1) \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & \\sim\\begin{bmatrix}-28 & -17 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
