    "question": {
      ":question/id": "3ca51266-03c7-5732-bbdc-4bb995a8b0c2",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $C,$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $C?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}$ means that we need to add $1$ times the first row to the third row.\n\n- The operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}$ means that we need to add $-3$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 7+(1)(-7) & 7+(1)(4) & 5+(1)(7)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 12\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 0+(-3)(-3) & 11+(-3)(-7) & 12+(-3)(8)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -7 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 32 & -12\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
